# How to cite the AIPolicyTracker dataset. GitHub shows a "Cite this repository"
# button from this file, and Zenodo reads .zenodo.json (kept in step with it) when it
# archives a tagged release. The records under data/ are CC BY 4.0; the code that
# serves them is Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE and data/LICENSE). Do not add a `doi` here
# until Zenodo has minted one; see docs/reference/releases.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it as below, together with the specific
  record URL, the date you accessed it and the official source the record links.
type: dataset
title: "AIPolicyTracker: a source-backed dataset of AI laws, policies, obligations and deadlines"
abstract: >-
  Structured, source-backed records of AI laws, regulations, strategies, standards
  and guidance across jurisdictions, with the obligations they impose, their
  deadlines, dated change events and the organisational controls that meet them.
  Every record links its official source and carries its review status, confidence
  level, last-verified date and the named reviewer who confirmed it. The data
  under data/ is licensed CC BY 4.0; the application source code is licensed
  Apache-2.0.
authors:
  - given-names: Bhaskar
    family-names: Bhatt
    email: bhaskar@aipolicytracker.org
    website: "https://bhaskar.com.np/"
contact:
  - given-names: Bhaskar
    family-names: Bhatt
    email: bhaskar@aipolicytracker.org
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/8h45k4r/aipolicytracker"
url: "https://aipolicytracker.org"
keywords:
  - AI regulation
  - AI policy
  - AI governance
  - AI law
  - EU AI Act
  - regulatory compliance
  - obligations
  - open data
